34,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found out that the household by the gate has complained the most, and some people aren't sure about turning away late bags. It seems like we really need a friendly solution!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I learned that the bin house at the station block can be quite smelly in the summer because it's hard to clean, and the supervised mornings next door take about fifty minutes each.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The installations clerk mentioned that a permanent build takes four months and requires five signatures, and each site change needs a new notice. Also, those supervised mornings take about fifty minutes.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I saw that the household by the gate filed almost all the complaints! Also, the frontages are all different sizes, and one is even blocked by a driveway. That's not fair!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"I have discovered that we spend thirty-four thousand yen annually on maintenance, and while a subsidy exists, the average cost for a shelter is quite high, around two hundred forty-eight thousand yen.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, that's a lot of money for a shelter! Maybe we should think about something that doesn't cost so much so everyone stays happy.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Kenji. If the cost is too high or the maintenance too difficult, it might create more tension between us rather than solving the problem.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, exactly. Beyond the money, the time commitment is a factor. If we choose a supervised system, we're looking at nearly an hour of work per turn, which could be a burden.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, but isn't that better than one person always having the bins at their gate? We have to make sure the work is shared equally, not just easy!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Rin, your spirit of fairness is commendable. However, we must ensure that the burden we share is one that every household can carry without causing new hardships.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I wonder if there's a way to make it fair without making anyone feel like they're being punished. Maybe we can find a middle ground that everyone likes!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I wonder if we can find a way to keep the area pleasant for everyone, especially in the heat, without making the rules too strict or the costs too high.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we consider the filing requirements, a rotating system seems logically complex due to the constant need for new notices, while a permanent build is a significant administrative and financial hurdle.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we just leave it where it is, the person at the gate keeps suffering! We can't just pick the easiest paperwork; we have to fix the unfairness.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, Rin. True harmony is not found in the path of least resistance, but in a solution where every neighbor feels seen and valued, regardless of their frontage or their purse.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I really hope we can all agree on something that makes everyone smile again. Let's look at the options and pick the one that keeps us the closest as neighbors!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Kenji. Let us look at the options with kindness and an open heart, keeping in mind both the physical space and the feelings of everyone involved.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will be looking for the option that balances administrative feasibility with a sustainable distribution of labor, as we cannot afford for one person to be overwhelmed.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'll be voting for whatever actually moves the bins or shares the work! No more letting one person do everything just because it's easier for the rest of us.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us remember that the most enduring agreements are those built on mutual respect and a shared sense of responsibility. I look forward to seeing which path we choose together.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
