60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Now that we see the options, I think we should pick one that makes everyone feel included and doesn't cause any more fighting! Which one do you all like best?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I'm worried about the Enclosed Structure because of the smells I heard about, and Managed Collection Hours sounds a bit strict. Perhaps Rotating Location is the gentlest way to share the burden?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Rotating Location seems problematic because of the filing requirements I discovered; each move requires a new notice. Managed Collection Hours is the most efficient, provided the schedule is strictly followed.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,Rotating Location is the only one that actually moves the bins! It's the only way to be truly fair to the person who has had them at their gate for years.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The Enclosed Structure is a heavy financial burden, and Managed Collection Hours may lead to conflict if neighbors cannot agree on turning away late bags. Rotating Location seems the most equitable.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, @Servas, and @Shizue all seem to like the Rotating Location! If it makes the person at the gate feel better and is fair, I'm happy with that too.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It does seem to be the most considerate choice, as it ensures no one person bears the burden alone for too long. I feel it would bring us closer.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, while it may seem considerate, the administrative burden of filing new notices for every rotation is inefficient. However, if the majority values fairness over paperwork, I will concede.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"I'm glad you're considering it, Asuka! Paperwork is just a few forms, but the unfairness of the bins staying in one spot is a problem we have to fix right now.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,It is often the case that a small amount of effort in administration is a worthy price to pay for the peace and dignity of our neighbors.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I think we've all found a way to agree! I'll vote for Rotating Location because it sounds like the best way to make sure everyone is happy and we stay friends.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I will also vote for Rotating Location. It feels like the most caring way to ensure that we all support one another and share the responsibility of our neighborhood.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I will vote for Rotating Location as well. While the administrative process is tedious, it is the only option that avoids both the high costs and the potential for interpersonal conflict.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,Rotating Location it is! I'm voting for it because it's the only way to make sure everyone takes a turn and no one is left out.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I shall cast my vote for Rotating Location as well. It is a path of shared burden and mutual understanding, which is the true foundation of a harmonious community.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
